From: slothfulchat <patches@slothfulchat.invalid>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 03:04:59 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] tests: integration tests against a madmail mock over webimap
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

DcTests/IntegrationTests drives the real UI controllers inside the
hosted test app, between real accounts on scripts/mock-madmail.mjs
(slothfulchat-web), reached at 127.0.0.1:8025 (MADMAIL_PORT overrides)
over plain HTTP through our core's webimap transport:

- onboarding: InstantOnboardingViewController with a
  `webimapaccount:` QR — type a name, tap "create", wait until the
  profile is configured on the mock
- send + receive: text typed into ChatViewController's composer and
  sent the way the paper-plane button does (draft.send()), received by
  the second account; then a reply lands in the first account's chat
- screenshot drop: an opaque snapshot of the chat window, dropped onto
  the composer through its real UIDropInteraction with a fake
  UIDropSession, gets staged as an image draft, sent, and received

Accounts are paired via vCards (keys included, no handshake) and are
tracked by id and removed when the suite ends, instead of being
flagged ui.ios.test_account, so DcTests' own cleanup can't delete
them mid-run.

PatchedCoreTests (offline, runs with the unit tests) checks that the
linked core parses `webimapaccount:` — upstream core does not, so a
pass proves the app links our patched core.

ChatViewController.draft goes from private to internal so the test can
type into the composer; it is the model the SwiftUI input bar binds to.

No network: everything talks to the local mock, so CI stays offline
and deterministic.
